    "careers-a-apply": "Find a role below and open it. Read what it asks for, then click \"Apply for this role.\" The form takes a few minutes, name, where you are, why this work matters to you, and your resume or a LinkedIn link.",
    "careers-a-cv": "Not always. For many volunteer and steward roles, a few honest sentences about why you want to help are enough. A LinkedIn link works in place of a formal CV.",
    "careers-a-where": "Our first sites are in northern Haiti, Milot, Fort-Liberté, and the towns around them. Many roles are on-site there; others (archive, translation, grants, governance) are fully remote. Each role card shows its location.",
    "careers-a-next": "A real person reviews every application. You'll get an email back. For paid and steward roles there's a conversation; for most volunteer roles we move quickly to scheduling your first day.",
    "careers-a-data": "Yes. We ask only for what we need to consider you, your information is encrypted, and you can ask us to delete it at any time. We never ask for bank details or ID numbers in an application.",
    "careers-assist-human": "Prefer a person? Write to careers@levoila.org.",
